IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://inprinthouston.org
 /wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Ayak-Akhtar-c-Vincent-Tullo-for-website.jpg
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://inprinthouston.org/wp-content/uploads/202
 6/07/Ayak-Akhtar-c-Vincent-Tullo-for-website.jpg
UID:U-aXbjGJfaC5hspOUw4KE
SUMMARY:Inprint Ayad Akhtar Reading
DTSTAMP:20260730T054953Z
DTSTART:20261005T193000Z
DESCRIPTION:General admission tickets will go on sale on Tuesday\, Septembe
	r 15\, 2026 at 12 pm. Season tickets are on sale here. \nAyad Akhtar will 
	read from his new novel The Radiance\, followed by an on-stage conversatio
	n led by a local author/journalist. The evening will conclude with a book 
	sale and signing. The event is presented as part of the 2026/2027 Inprint 
	Margarett Root Brown Reading Series.  \nPulitzer Prize winner Ayad Akhtar’
	s new novel The Radiance is “simply put\, a work of genius. Through unforg
	ettable characters Akhtar explores the nature of memory and of the soul\, 
	while the unfolding tale builds tension and anticipation like a whodunit” 
	(Abraham Verghese). It has been named one of the New York Time‘s “Novels E
	veryone Will Be Talking About in 2026.” A mysterious accident along a coun
	try road sparks an awakening and an investigation in Akhtar’s most daring 
	work yet—a visionary novel of spiritual transformation in an age of fractu
	re. \nAkhtar’s work as a novelist and playwright has been published and pe
	rformed in over two dozen languages. He is the winner of the Pulitzer Priz
	e for Drama for his play Disgraced\, which was also nominated for the Tony
	 Award for Best Play. His other Broadway plays include McNeal\, Junk\, and
	 The Who & The What. Akhtar is also the author of the novels American Derv
	ish\, a Kirkus Reviews Best Book of the Year\, and Homeland Elegies\, call
	ed “a tour de force” by The Washington Post. In 2021\, he was named the Ne
	w York State Author by the New York State Writers Institute\, succeeding C
	olson Whitehead. \n\n\nhttps://inprinthouston.org/event/inprint-ayad-akhta
	r-reading/\n\nFrom Inprint Houston
URL:https://inprinthouston.org/event/inprint-ayad-akhtar-reading/
LOCATION:Alley Theatre\, 615 Texas Avenue\, Houston\, TX\, 77002
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:inprint-houston
CATEGORIES:Inprint Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
