UID:Jz24G5kzpSySjgbe4M5wX
SUMMARY:Across Two Seas Symposium
DTSTAMP:20260730T054953Z
DTSTART:20261008T150000Z
DESCRIPTION:Across Two Seas brings together scholars\, curators\, artists\,
	 and community members for a multi-day symposium at Rice University on Bla
	ck subjectivities across the medieval and early modern Mediterranean\, Isl
	amic world\, and Indian Ocean. Through panels\, film screenings\, public c
	onversations\, and interdisciplinary dialogue\, the symposium explores how
	 Black subjects were represented in artistic\, literary\, and documentary 
	sources and how these representations were shaped by trade\, travel\, reli
	gion\, knowledge-making\, and cultural exchange. By connecting Europe\, No
	rth Africa\, the Arabian Peninsula\, East Africa\, India\, and Southeast A
	sia\, Across Two Seas expands the geography of premodern race studies and 
	places the Indian Ocean at the center of conversations too often framed pr
	imarily through Europe. The symposium invites broader publics to consider 
	how histories of Blackness were made across multiple regions\, media\, and
	 worlds.\n\nhttps://events.rice.edu/art-history/event/433862-across-two-se
	as-symposium\n\nFrom Rice University - Open to the Public
URL:https://events.rice.edu/art-history/event/433862-across-two-seas-sympos
	ium
GEO:29.7174;-95.4018
LOCATION:Moody Center
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:rice-public-events
CATEGORIES:Rice University - Open to the Public
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT8H
END:VEVENT
